In this task, we will be discussing a study on the vulnerability of LLM-MASs (Large Language Models for Multi-Agent Systems) to blocking attacks and propose mitigation strategies. The paper presents an attack paradigm called CORBA that can block language models in large language model systems by injecting malicious prompts, leading to a significant security threat. Extensive experiments demonstrate the vulnerability of existing open-source frameworks and open-ended simulations. We confirm that the proposed mitigations will benefit the application of LLM-MASs in the real world. In light of the abnormal consumption of resources caused by blocking attacks, monitoring resources might be a promising method to protect LLM-MASs. Consequently, in future works, we will further investigate effective defense mechanisms to prevent such blocking attacks in LLM-MASs.
